<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huaihai campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Xuzhou · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Huaihai campaign was one of the three decisive campaigns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a>, fought from November 1948 to January 1949 in the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuzhou">Xuzhou</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huai-river">Huai River</a> and the Longhai railway. Communist armies under Liu Bocheng, Chen Yi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deng-xiaoping">Deng Xiaoping</a> destroyed or captured several Nationalist armies, some half a million men, opening the way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huaihai-campaign.jpg" alt="Huaihai campaign" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PLAHuaihai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
